    "id": "workflow",
    "title": "GreatPM Workflow",
    "markdown": "# GreatPM product workflow\n\nGreatPM organizes product work into a continuous six-stage loop:\n\n1. **Discover** — establish the problem with customer and market evidence.\n2. **Strategize** — choose the customer, position, advantage, and measurable\n   outcome.\n3. **Prioritize** — compare opportunities and make explicit tradeoffs.\n4. **Define** — turn the selected opportunity into testable requirements,\n   success metrics, risks, and non-goals.\n5. **Launch** — prepare rollout, communications, support, observability, and\n   rollback.\n6. **Measure** — compare outcomes with the committed targets, capture learning,\n   and feed the evidence into the next discovery cycle.\n\n## Operating principles\n\n- Start with evidence, not a predetermined feature.\n- Keep assumptions visibly separate from verified facts.\n- Use the smallest method that can answer the current decision.\n- Make acceptance criteria and success thresholds testable.\n- Preserve dissent, risks, and unresolved decisions in the artifact.\n- Treat launch as the start of measurement, not the end of the workflow.\n- Require a person to approve consequential strategy, scope, and launch\n  decisions.\n\nThe remote MCP server can recommend methods and prepare this workflow. It does\nnot execute stages, access a project, contact other systems, or make approvals."
